WEBVTT

00:00:02.800 --> 00:00:06.805
[Cat] Lesson one. What an AI tool can and cannot do.

00:00:07.205 --> 00:00:16.052
[Cat] This review draft uses real ChatGPT screenshots, annotated. Screenshots, not a continuous live recording.

00:00:16.452 --> 00:00:22.141
[Cat] Blank product page. You know this mug. You just need a first sentence.

00:00:22.541 --> 00:00:24.863
[Pom] Okay… but do I have to know coding for this?

00:00:25.263 --> 00:00:31.660
[Cat] No. Today we write a clear ask, then decide what to keep. Coding can wait.

00:00:32.060 --> 00:00:39.328
[Cat] People often start with a vague ask. Here is a real ChatGPT capture from a logged-out chat.

00:00:39.728 --> 00:00:43.002
[Cat] Exact ask: Write something about my mug.

00:00:43.402 --> 00:00:46.177
[Pom] That sounds finished already. Is it wrong?

00:00:46.577 --> 00:00:59.197
[Cat] Not necessarily wrong. It is generic creative copy — warm and fluent. But notice: it never used colour, material, or size, because we never gave those facts.

00:00:59.597 --> 00:01:04.357
[Cat] Same mug. Only the facts we actually have for practice.

00:01:04.757 --> 00:01:13.105
[Cat] Confirmed facts: green ceramic mug. Capacity: three hundred fifty milliliters. Nothing else supplied.

00:01:13.505 --> 00:01:15.769
[Pom] So we ask again, with those facts?

00:01:16.169 --> 00:01:21.335
[Cat] Yes. Another real capture — a fresh chat, one clearer ask.

00:01:21.735 --> 00:01:34.529
[Cat] We asked for four short lines, using only green ceramic mug and three hundred fifty milliliters. No inventing price, shipping, reviews, care, or customer quotes.

00:01:34.929 --> 00:01:40.316
[Pom] It used green, ceramic, and three hundred fifty milliliters. Good.

00:01:40.716 --> 00:01:55.437
[Cat] Right. It also added friendly promotional wording — like favourite drinks, and everyday drinkware collection. That is subjective tone, not a secret product fact. We do not call those hallucinations here.

00:01:55.837 --> 00:01:57.091
[Pom] So… keep everything?

00:01:57.491 --> 00:02:04.736
[Cat] You decide. A clearer prompt helps, but it still is not a guarantee of truth. You still review.

00:02:05.136 --> 00:02:19.985
[Cat] Optional human edit — labelled as ours, not as the AI reply. Keep the known facts in plain words: a green ceramic mug, capacity three hundred fifty milliliters, simple and friendly.

00:02:20.385 --> 00:02:23.137
[Pom] So the tool drafts, and I judge.

00:02:23.537 --> 00:02:37.074
[Cat] Right. Fluent does not mean guaranteed true. Different tools and settings differ. Logged-out ChatGPT worked for these screenshots today — that can vary by region or network.

00:02:37.474 --> 00:02:41.677
[Pom] If I ask are you sure, and it says yes — is that a check?

00:02:42.077 --> 00:02:49.600
[Cat] That is the same tool agreeing with itself. Checking means matching the words to facts you know.

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:53.413
[Pom] Got it. Clear facts in. Review what comes out.

00:02:53.813 --> 00:02:58.852
[Cat] That’s Lesson one. For now — one useful draft, your judgment.

00:02:59.252 --> 00:03:04.639
[Cat] Pause here if you want. Which words must come from the facts we supplied?

00:03:06.139 --> 00:03:16.669
[Cat] Green, ceramic, and three hundred fifty milliliters. Friendly tone words are optional. Anything else factual needs your say-so first.

00:03:17.069 --> 00:03:24.894
[Cat] Review draft. Real ChatGPT screenshots, annotated. Screenshots, not a continuous live recording.

00:03:25.294 --> 00:03:33.816
[Cat] The full exercise stays in the written lesson. This is not lip-sync animation or live practice inside the site.
